2.
Definitions
- .In these rules, unless the context otherwise requires,
(a)
Act means the Control of National Highways(Land and Traffic) Act, 2002 (
13 of 2003
);
(b)
appellant means a person making an appeal to the Tribunal under section 14;
(c)
appeal means an appeal made to the Tribunal under section 14;
(d)
legal practitioner shall have the meaning assigned to it in the Advocates Act, 1961 (25 of 1961);
(e)
Presiding Officer means the Presiding Officer of a Tribunal;
(f)
Registrar means the Registrar of a Tribunal;
(g)
Registry means the Registry of a Tribunal;
(h)
section means a section of the Act;
(i)
Tribunal means the National Highways Tribunal established under sub-section (1) of section 5;
(j)
the words and expressions used and not defined in these rules but are defined in the Act shall have the same meaning
as respectively assigned to them in the Act.
